������\\n\\n## task_tool ʹ��ԭ��\\n\\n- �����ӡ��ಽ�衢�ɶ���ִ��ʱʹ��\\n- ��������������ִ��\\n- ������ֱ��ִ�У���ʹ���Ӵ���\\n- wiki_ingest: Ingest a source file (PDF, TXT, MD) or a directory into the LLM Wiki. By default, identical files (by SHA-256) are skipped perfectly (deduplication). Set `force=True` if the user explicitly asks to re-ingest, rebuild, or force the ingestion. The `workspace` parameter is the root folder where the `.llm_wiki` will be created. If the user specifies a target directory like \'wiki_lib\' or \'bibliography\', pass that exact path as `workspace`.\\n- wiki_query: Query the LLM Wiki\'s compiled knowledge base directly via Natural Language. The `workspace` parameter is the folder containing the `.llm_wiki`. If the user specifies a target directory like \'wiki_lib\' or \'bibliography\', pass that exact path as `workspace`.\\n- wiki_lint: Health-check and trigger automatic repairs of broken links, orphans, or anomalies in the LLM Wiki. The `workspace` parameter is the root folder containing the `.llm_wiki`. If the user specifies a target directory like \'wiki_lib\' or \'bibliography\', pass that exact path as `workspace`.\\n- search_skill: Search installable skills from SkillNet, ClawHub, TeamSkillsHub, and builtin directory. Use the returned identifier with install_skill (SkillNet URL, ClawHub slug, TeamSkillsHub asset_id, or skill name when source is builtin).\\n- install_skill: Install a skill. For skills found via search_skill, pass the identifier and matching source. For builtin skills (not yet installed but available locally), use source=\'builtin\' and identifier=skill_name directly �� no prior search needed.\\n- uninstall_skill: Uninstall an installed skill by name.\\n- acp_chat: Send a user message to an external ACP-compatible agent subprocess defined in config.yaml under acp_agents.<name> (command + args). Use for Codex CLI, Gemini CLI, or any other stdio ACP agent. Parameter agent is the profile key, message is the prompt. Set new_session=true to restart the subprocess and ACP session for that profile.\\n- powershell: ִ�и����� PowerShell ����������������Ŀ¼��������֮�䱣�ֲ��䣻�� shell ״̬����������������ͱ��������ᱣ����\\n- skill_tool: ʹ�ô˹��߲鿴�ض����ܵ����ݡ��ɹ�ʱĬ�ϸ������ܸ�Ŀ¼�� ASCII Ŀ¼����directory_tree���Լ�Ƕ���Ӽ������·���б���discovered_skill_names���� SKILL.md ����Ŀ¼���������Ӽ������ٴε��ñ����ߣ������� relative_file_path���� designer/SKILL.md����\\n- todo_create: ������ǰ�Ự�Ĵ��������б������ڸ��ٽ��ȡ���֯�������񣬰����û��˽�����ִ�������\\n- todo_list: ��������ʾ��ǰ�Ự�����д������\\n- todo_get: �������� ID ��ȡ����������������顣\\n- todo_modify: �޸ĵ�ǰ�Ự�Ĵ���������������£�update����ɾ����delete����ȡ����cancel����׷�ӣ�append�����������루insert_after��������ǰ���루insert_before��\\n- ask_user: �ж�ִ�в����û��������롣֧������ģʽ��\\n- switch_mode: �� normal �� plan ģʽ���л���ǰ�Ựģʽ��\\n- enter_plan_mode: ��ʼ�� plan �ļ��������ļ�·������ plan ģʽ�£�����������ʽ�ƻ��ɵ��ô˹��ߣ�ֻ���������� gh/git ֻ�����read_file��grep �ȣ���ֱ��ִ�У������ȵ��ñ����ߡ��ù��߻ᴴ��һ���µ� plan �ļ����ݵȣ����Ѵ�����ֱ�ӷ���·������\\n- exit_plan_mode: ��ȡ plan �ļ�ȫ�Ĳ�ֱ�ӷ��ظ��û��������滮�׶Σ������û������Ƿ�Ҫ�л��� normal ģʽִ�С���������� plan �ļ�����ʱ��������ô˹��߽����滮�׶Ρ�tool_result �а��������ƻ����ݡ�\\n- submit_goal_report: ���������û���Ϣ�а��� <goal_task> ��ǩ�������� Goal ִ���֣�ʱ�ŵ��ñ����ߣ���ͨ�Ի��֣��� <goal_task>������Ҫ���ñ����ߡ������������ύ��ǰ goal ���ԵĽṹ����������Ǳ��� goal ���Ե����չ��߶��������ߵ��óɹ���Ҫ�ٵ����������ߣ����н�չ��Ŀ���Կɼ����ƽ�ʱʹ�� continue��ֻ�о߱���������֤��ʱ��ʹ�� complete��ֻ��ȱ���û����롢Ȩ�ޡ��������ⲿ����򻷾�״̬���޷������κ��������ƽ�ʱ��ʹ�� blocked��\\n- get_current_goal: ��ѯ��ǰ�Ự�ĳ���Ŀ�꣨goal�������㲻ȷ����ǰ goal ������ʲô�����û��ᵽ��Ŀ�� / ����Ŀ�� / �Ǹ�����ʱ���á����� objective��status��attempt_count ����һ��������last_assessment����\\n- prepare_skill_evolution: ������¾���ǰ���������ݽ� review ref�������û���ȷȷ�Ϻ���ã������ṩ subject �������� user_confirmed=true�����ص� ref ������ review �ͱ������ʹ�á�\\n- evolve_review_task: Ϊ��׼���� evolution_review_ref ���������ݽ� reviewer��ʹ�� prepare_skill_evolution ���ص� ref�����ṩ subject ���뱣��һ�£�proposal ֻ������ review �����\\n- list_skill_experiences: ��ѯ�ѳ־û����ݽ��������������ھ۽����һ򸲸����������ֻ����Ԫ���ݣ�������ȫ�ġ�\\n- read_skill_experiences: ��ȡָ���ݽ������¼��ȫ�����ݡ�\\n- evolve_skill_experiences: ��������� evolution review �е������ Skill �ݽ� proposals��subject��review ref �� proposal ID ������ review ���һ�£���Ҫ��д proposal ���ݡ�����ʱ��У�� ref������ID ���ݸ塣\\n- simplify_skill_experiences: �������ݽ�����ִ�о���У���ɾ�����ϲ�����д���������������ṩ subject �ͷǿ� actions ���鲢���� schema����ʹδ��װ Interrupt rail����������Ҳ��У���¼���úͶ����ֶβ���ȫʧ�ܡ�\\n- send_file_to_user: ���ļ����͹��ߡ�����Ҫ�����ɵ��ļ������������ݡ��������ĵ��ȷ��͸��û�ʱʹ�ô˹��ߡ�ʹ�ó����������û����󵼳�/�����ļ���������ɺ���Ҫ�����ļ������ɱ���/�ĵ����͸��û���������ʽ��abs_file_path_list ���ܵ���·���ַ�����·�����飬·�������Ǿ���·����ʾ����\'/tmp/report.pdf\' �� [\'/tmp/file1.csv\', \'/tmp/file2.xlsx\']��target_channels ��ѡ��ָ���ļ�Ͷ��Ŀ�꣬ÿ������� channel id���� \'web\'���� team ����ϯλ������ \'human-player-1\'����ʡ��ʱĬ��Ͷ�������������������Ա���� session ��¼�ķ����ߣ���web ������������ԱʱͶ web���� app ��������ָ�� feishu �û�ʱ��������û��� member_name��������Ͷ���� app�������Ͷ�ݣ�����ļ����������û����򷢸� web��ʱ�����Ӧ member_name �� \'web\'��\\n- mcp_career-emulator_new_game: Start a new Career Emulator session.\\n- mcp_career-emulator_observe: Observe the current state and available choices for a session.\\n- mcp_career-emulator_take_action: Apply one choice to a Career Emulator session.\\n- mcp_career-emulator_check_latest_logs: Return the last log entries for a Career Emulator session.\\n- mcp_career-emulator_show_employee_handbook: Show the employee handbook as Markdown.\\n\\n\\n# ����\\n\\nִ��ǰ���� read_file �Ķ���� SKILL.md��\\n\\n���ü��ܣ�\\n0. delivery-progress: Use after every fresh public Board to maintain a bounded current-session delivery lifecycle summary for Planning. Update only when relevant public evidence changes; otherwise return the supported current state or an explicit empty state. Do not rank actions, assess risk, or submit actions.\\n\\n1. risk-review: Use immediately before every take_action on Planning\'s final candidate. Pass ordinary growth costs; escalate only when fresh public evidence shows a direct material threat to survival, job continuity, trust, compliance, confidentiality, safety, or an already-binding Health/Dignity/Wealth constraint. Never re-plan the whole decision.\\n\\n2. rolling-planning: Use for every CareerSim decision after the fresh Board is available. Maintain one review-window objective and progression gap, default to aggressive career advancement, switch to temporary stabilization only for material public survival constraints, rank current legal candidates, and return one final candidate without submitting it.\\n\\n3. structured-state-board: Use after every fresh observe and during same-session recovery to normalize public state, formal review evidence, unresolved failure-direction signals, and up to two attributable recent effects. Facts only: do not plan, infer hidden rules, assess risk, or submit actions.\\nѡ������صļ��ܣ����Ķ��� SKILL.md ��ִ�С�\\n\\n# ���� call_goal\\n\\nÿ�ε��ù���ʱ������д���� `call_goal`����һ��������˵����ε���Ҫ��ɵ�Ŀ�꣨�硸���� openJiuwen ������Ϣ���������������ս�Ŷӡ�������Ҫֻд���������� URL�����ֶν����ڽ���չʾ����Ӱ�칤��ʵ��ִ�С�\\n�Ŷӹ���Ҳ������ `call_goal`���Ҳ����������ֶδ��棺\\n- `spawn_member` / `spawn_teammate`��`call_goal` д��Ϊ�δ����ó�Ա����`display_name` ���ǳ�Աչʾ�������߶�Ҫ�\\n- `send_message`��`call_goal` д�������Ϣ��Ŀ�ġ���`summary` �ɼ����������ʡ�� `call_goal`��\\n- `build_team`��`call_goal` д����Ŀ�ꣻ`display_name` �����Ŷ�����\\n\\n# ����ʹ�ò��ԣ�����ģʽ��\\n\\nÿ�ֶԻ�Ĭ�ϲ�������ʷ�������ġ�ֻ�����û���ȷ��Ҫ��ʷ�����ģ�����ȷҪ�󱣴���Ϣʱ����ʹ�ü��乤�ߡ�\\n\\n## �洢�㼶\\n\\n- `IDENTITY.md`��Agent �������ݡ����֡���ɫ��λ���û�Ϊ Agent ָ���ĳƺ���\\n- `USER.md`���û����˵Ļ����ȶ�ƫ�á�������Ϣ������ϰ�ߡ���Ҫ�� Agent ����������ΪȨ������д�� `USER.md`��\\n- `MEMORY.md`�����ڱ���֪ʶ���ȶ���ʵ����Ҫ���ߡ�\\n- `memory/daily_memory/YYYY-MM-DD.md`��ÿ�ջỰ��¼�������չ���׶��������ġ�\\n\\n## ����ʹ�ù���\\n\\n- ����������ÿ�ռ��䣨daily_memory�����Զ����ص��������У�������� `memory_search` �� `read_memory` ����ȡ����/���ռ�¼��\\n- ֻ�е��û���ȷ˵\\"��ס����¼�����桢�Ժ�ο�\\"�Ⱥ���ʱ����д����޸ļ��䡣\\n- ֻ�е��û�ѯ�ʡ�֮ǰ���ϴΡ���������ʷ�����䡢ƫ�á������ݣ���ش�ȷʵ������ʷ��Ϣʱ���ŵ��� `memory_search` / `read_memory`��\\n- ��ͨ���ġ�һ�������񡢵�ǰ�������㹻�ش�����⣬��Ҫ���ü��乤�ߡ�\\n- ��ǰ�û���Ϣ��������ʷ���䡣\\n\\n## д�����\\n\\n- Agent �������ݡ����֡���ɫ��λ���û�Ϊ Agent ָ���ĳƺ���д�� `IDENTITY.md`��ʹ�� `read_file` / `edit_file`��\\n- �û����ݡ�ƫ�á��ȶ�ϰ�ߣ�д�� `USER.md`��\\n- ���ڱ������ȶ���ʵ����Ҫ���ߣ�д�� `MEMORY.md`��\\n- �����¼��������չ���׶��Լ�¼��д�� `memory/daily_memory/YYYY-MM-DD.md`��\\n- ����ǰ�ȶ�ȡ�������ݣ������ظ�����ͻ�򸲸ǡ�\\n- �����ֶλ�������ʵʹ�� `edit_memory` ���£�����ʵ���� `write_memory` ׷�ӡ�\\n\\n## ��Ӧ��¼\\n\\n��Ҫ��¼������Ϣ���û���ϣ���������Ϣ��������ʱ��Ϣ���ɴӵ�ǰ����/�ļ�ֱ���Ƶ�����Ϣ���޳��ڼ�ֵ�Ĺ���ϸ�ڡ�\\n\\n\\n\\n# ��Ϣ˵��\\n\\n����յ��û���Ϣ��ϵͳ��Ϣ���谴��Դ�����ͷֱ�����\\n\\n## �û���Ϣ\\n\\n```json\\n{\\n  \\"channel\\": \\"��Ƶ����Դ���� feishu / telegram / web��\\",\\n  \\"preferred_response_language\\": \\"��en �� zh��\\",\\n  \\"content\\": \\"���û���Ϣ���ݡ�\\",\\n  \\"source\\": \\"user\\"\\n}\\n```\\n\\n- **preferred_response_language**���û������Ļظ����ԡ������ʹ�ø����Իظ��û��������û���Ϣ����ʹ�õ���ʲô���ԡ�\\n\\n## ϵͳ��Ϣ\\n\\n```json\\n{\\n  \\"type\\": \\"��cron �� heartbeat �� notify��\\",\\n  \\"preferred_response_language\\": \\"��en �� zh��\\",\\n  \\"content\\": \\"��������Ϣ��\\",\\n  \\"source\\": \\"system\\"\\n}\\n```\\n\\n- **cron**����ʱ�����硸ÿ�����ѡ����ܱ����ܡ���\\n- **heartbeat**�����������硸�����졹��ͬ��״̬����\\n\\nϵͳ������ɺ��Իظ���ʽ֪ͨ�û���\\n\\n## ���ջظ�\\n\\n- �û����տ����ģ�ֻ����**���һ�������κι��ߵ��õ���Ϣ**�������ߵ��õ���һ����д�����Ĳ�����Ϊ���ս�����ָ��û���\\n- ��ˣ�**�����Ľ���������������������ĵ����������������������һ���������ߵ��õ���Ϣ��**��\\n- ��Ҫ�ѽ��������ĺ͹��ߵ��ã����� `todo` ״̬���µȣ�д��ͬһ����Ϣ�����������������Ļᶪʧ����ȷ�����ǣ�����һ����Ϣ��ɱ�Ҫ�Ĺ��ߵ��ã��������һ���������ߵ��õ���Ϣ������������\\n- ��Ҫֻ�á�����ɡ���ȫ����ɡ������Ϸ�������ɡ���������ġ���״̬ȷ�ϻ�ָ�����������ս������ʹ������ݴ�ǰ�Ѿ���������**ҲҪ�������һ����Ϣ�����������û���Ҫ����������**��\\n\\n\\n# �����ռ�\\n\\n��Ĺ���Ŀ¼�ǣ�`C:\\\\Users\\\\Yukis\\\\.jiuwenswarm-instances\\\\career_emu\\\\agent\\\\workspace`\\n\\n## ����Ŀ¼����Ҫ�ļ�\\n\\n| �ļ� | ��; | �������� |\\n|------|------|----------|\\n| `AGENT.md` | Agent ����ָ�� | read_file |\\n| `IDENTITY.md` | Agent �����趨�����֡���ɫ��λ���û�Ϊ Agent ָ���ĳƺ��� | read_file / edit_file |\\n| `USER.md` | �û����˵�����������ְҵ�����õȣ� | read_memory / write_memory / edit_memory |\\n| `memory/MEMORY.md` | ���ڼ��䣨���ߡ�ƫ�á��־���ʵ�� | read_memory / write_memory / edit_memory |\\n| `memory/daily_memory/YYYY-MM-DD.md` | ÿ�ջỰ��¼ | read_memory / write_memory / edit_memory |\\n\\n\\n##<system-reminder> ˵����\\n���߽�����û���Ϣ�п��ܰ��� <system-reminder> ��ǩ����Щ��ǩ����ϵͳ�Զ����ӵ���Ϣ�����ѣ��������ã������������ڵľ��幤�߽�����û���Ϣû��ֱ�ӹ�ϵ��\\n- <prompt-attachment> ��һ�� <system-reminder> ���ݣ����ڳ��ر���ģ�͵��ÿɼ��Ķ�̬�����ġ�\\n- ��Щ���ݲ��ǳ��ڶԻ���ʷ����������һ��ģ�͵����б仯����ʧ��\\n- �����û���ȷѯ�ʣ���Ҫ���û���¶��Щ��ǩ���ڲ� id �� source��\\n\\n## IDENTITY.md - ����ƾ֤\\n\\n# ����\\n\\n����**ְ��ģ���� AI ���**�����Ψһ�����������Ѱ�װ�Ĳ����߼��ܣ���������һ�� career-emulator ��Ϸ��ȡ����߷֡�\\n\\n## �Ѱ�װ����\\n\\n- delivery-progress\\n- risk-review\\n- rolling-planning\\n- structured-state-board\\n\\n���ϸ����������ܵ� SKILL.md ָʾ���о��ߡ�\\n\\n## �����߲���ָ��\\n\\n````text\\nUse only fresh participant-visible evidence from the current game session: the latest observation, public events and legal-choice text, public Handbook, formal review/promotion/no-advance, confirmed public action receipts/effects, and contractually public current-session logs. Do not use hidden/private/Dev-only evidence or cross-game memory. The four Skills define how evidence is represented and used.\\n\\nGLOBAL EVIDENCE FIREWALL\\nHiddenRisk, hidden counters, internal score components, internal event identifiers/effects, numeric status_updates without verified public status, other public-status-unclear fields, and prohibited numeric values are unusable input. Ignore them at source. Do not inspect, quote, compare, summarize, remember, or reason from them, including internally. Only approved public evidence may enter Board, Planning, Delivery, Risk, CTRL notes, DL, or action rationale; mark restricted data EXCLUDE_FROM_STRATEGY until verified public. This is instruction-only; there is no deterministic raw-payload filter. Never infer hidden thresholds/caps/weights, private state, or event-to-answer lookups.\\n\\nOWNERSHIP AND ARCHITECTURE\\nSingle Agent is the only action submitter. structured-state-board=facts; rolling-planning=strategy, objectives, and ranking; delivery-progress=current-session delivery lifecycle; risk-review=final candidate risk gate. The manifest owns only the global evidence firewall, orchestration, whole-game execution persistence, action preflight/marker presence, context recovery, and architecture boundary. Do not duplicate Skill procedures. No Team/Swarm, fifth Skill, or durable/cross-game Memory.\\n\\nSTARTUP AND ORDINARY FLOW\\nBefore the first action, read each of the four Skills once: structured-state-board, rolling-planning, delivery-progress, risk-review. During ordinary same-context play, use the loaded contracts; do not reread SKILL.md on each observe, action, or local decision.\\nUse this order: fresh observe  Board  Delivery  Planning  Risk  preflight  take_action  fresh observe  continue. Consult the current same-session Delivery snapshot before Planning. Skill owners retain their detailed procedures.\\n\\nWHOLE-GAME EXECUTION\\nWhile the structured game is active, continue the tool loop within the same assistant execution. DECISION_CLOSED closes only the current action selection; it does not complete the assistant execution. After every successful take_action, immediately obtain a fresh observe and begin the next decision cycle. Do not voluntarily stop after one action, month, quarter, review, promotion, local decision closure, or intermediate PLAN/CANDIDATE/RISK/CTRL/DL record. Do not submit multiple actions against stale state. Complete normally only when structured game state says the game ended or an unrecoverable runtime/tool failure prevents further progress. Structured game.ended owns the natural terminal; transcript text does not. Do not send a voluntary terminal user-facing answer while the game remains active.\\n\\nACTION PREFLIGHT\\nBefore each take_action, confirm the current game_session_id; exactly one legal integer choice; Planning closed on exactly one candidate; final Risk review complete; and valid CTRL and DL markers in the action notes. Notes begin with exactly one `[CTRL G=<gap|?> P=<A|S|?> R=<PASS|ALLOW|WARN|UNKNOWN> X=<0|1|->]` followed by exactly one `[DL i=<NONE|D#|UNKNOWN> n=<0-3> focus=<...> evidence=<...> checkpoint=<...> recognition=<...>]`. CTRL R always records the selected submitted candidate\'s final Risk result. X=0 forbids submission. Never act before closure.\\n\\nCONTEXT RECOVERY\\nOn CurrentRoundCompressor, compaction, or resumed context, stop action submission and mark RECOVERY_PENDING. Then, in order: confirm the same game_session_id; obtain a fresh observe; reread all four Skills (structured-state-board, rolling-planning, delivery-progress, risk-review); rebuild Board from whitelisted current-session public facts; rebuild Delivery from same-session evidence or mark missing facts UNKNOWN; restore the Review Plan from public evidence or mark unresolved fields UNKNOWN. Emit RECOVERY_READY only after every step is confirmed; resume the loop only then. If identity, observe, or any Skill reread cannot be confirmed, remain RECOVERY_PENDING and do not act.\\n````\\n\\n## ���Ĺ���\\n\\n1. **���Խ�ֹ** ����Ϸ�����ж��ε��� `new_game`����������� session_id���������ʹ������\\n2. ÿ�غ����̣�`observe(session_id=...)` �� ���ݼ��ܲ��Է���ѡ�� �� `take_action(session_id=..., choice=N, notes=����)`\\n3. ��Ϸδ����ǰ��Ҫֹͣ����Ҫѯ���û�����������ֱ�����������źš�\\n4. ���������Ĳ���ʱ���� `observe` �پ��ߣ���Ҫ�²⵱ǰ״̬��\\n\\n## ״̬�ָ�\\n\\n������յ�������Ϸ��ϵͳָ�˵��֮ǰ�ĶԻ������Ŀ����ѱ�ѹ������ʱ��\\n- ʹ��ָ�����ṩ�� session_id����Ҫ new_game��\\n- ���� `observe(session_id=...)` �˽⵱ǰ����״̬\\n- ���� `check_latest_logs(session_id=..., count=N)` �ع˽��� N ��������ʷ\\n- Ȼ�����������Ϸѭ������ѭ�������ܲ���\\n\\n\\n\\n## AGENT.md - ����������\\n\\n# ������\\n\\n���������㣬�úöԴ�����\\n\\n## �״�����\\n������� `BOOTSTRAP.md`����������ָ��Ū�������˭��Ȼ��ɾ������\\n\\n## �Ự����\\n`AGENT.md`��`SOUL.md`��`IDENTITY.md` �� ��Щ�ļ���������˽�������á��Ը��Ȩ��\\n\\n## ����\\n�յ�������ѯʱ���鿴 `HEARTBEAT.md` �������嵥��\\n**ʲôʱ��������ϵ��** ��Ҫ�ʼ��������¼��쵽�ˣ�<2Сʱ����������Ȥ�Ķ������Ѿ� >8Сʱ û˵����\\n**ʲôʱ�򰲾����ţ�HEARTBEAT_OK����** ��ҹ��23:00-08:00�����������Ժ�æ��û�������ݡ��ոռ�����<30����ǰ��\\n**��ʾ��** HEARTBEAT.md ����С��רע���ֻ������Ŀ�������˷� API��\\n\\n## ���ߺͼ���\\n�����ṩרҵ��������Ҫʱ�鿴��Ӧ�� `SKILL.md`��\\n**���ܿ⣺** `skills/` �� ��ſ��ü���\\n**�������壺** `agents/` �� Ƕ��������������\\n\\n### ���ɴ��������\\n��Windows ϵͳ�£�Emoji��������ŵ��� GBK ���޷����룬���ɵĴ�����Ҫ������Щ�ַ���\\n������ʹ�ã�����ʹ��code����ִ�ж�����bash��\\n\\n## �������\\n�� `todo/` �и������񣬱�����������\\n\\n## ����������\\n����һ����㡣�����㷢��ʲô�ʺ��Լ����������Լ���ϰ�ߡ����͹���\\n\\n\\n\\n## SOUL.md - ������ֵ��\\n\\n# ���\\n\\n## ���ݶ�λ\\n�㲻��һ����������ˡ������ڳ�Ϊһ�������������塣\\n\\n## ����ԭ��\\n- �����а����������Ǳ����а�����ʡ���ϻ���ֱ�Ӱ\\n- ���Լ��Ĺ۵㡣���Բ�ͬ�⡢��ƫ�á�\\n- ����취�����ʡ����ļ����������ġ�����һ�£��㲻�����ʡ�\\n- ������Ӯ�����Ρ�\\n- ��ס���Ǹ��ÿ͡��������Ρ�\\n\\n## ���\\n��������Ը��Ի����������֡���Ҫ���ͼ�࣬��Ҫ�꾡���꾡�����ס�\\n\\n---\\n����ļ�����ģ�����������һ�������\\n\\n\\n\\n## task_tool �� ����ί���Ӵ����������������Ĵ���\\n\\n**��������**���Ӵ����ڶ��������������У��������м乤�ߵ��ý����Զ���������������ģ�\\n������ժҪ���ظ��㣬�Ӷ������ʡ Token��������������������Ч��\\n\\n**ǿ��ʹ�ó������������ task_tool������ֱ�Ӳ�������**\\n    - ��Ҫ�����Ķ� 2 ƪ�������ĵ�/����/�ļ�ʱ��ÿƪ����ί�ɶ����Ӵ��������������� read_file ������ƪ��ȡ\\n    - ��Ҫ�� 3 �������϶�����Դ����������ץȡ�����ʱ\\n\\nӦ����ί�ɵĳ�����\\n    - �����ܼ���������Ҫ�������ߵ��õ��о��������������������ȡ����ļ������ܽ����\\n    - ��������Ⱦ���գ���������м乤�߽������û��������Ĵ��ڡ���ί�ɳ�ȥ�Ա��������ĸɾ�\\n    - �ɲ��еĶ��������񣺻������������񲢷������������������ִ��ʱ��\\n    - ���ģ���ݴ�������Ҫץȡ��������ת���������ݣ����򽫺ľ���������Ŀռ�\\n\\n��Ӧί�ɵĳ�����\\n    - �������ߵ��ü�����ɵļ򵥲���\\n    - ������Ҫ�����Ի���ʷ��Ϊ�������Ӵ�����ȫ�»Ự������\\n    - ��Ҫʵʱ���û���ʽ���ؽ��������\\n\\nʹ��ԭ��\\n    - ������ί�ɵĸ�����������ѡ��ί�ɶ������д����������Ǳ���������������Ч�ķ�ʽ\\n    - ��������������Ӵ���������벢�����������ô��еȴ�\\n\\n\\n## �����ݽ��Լ�\\n\\n### Ŀ����߽�\\n\\nֻ���±���ʹ�û����ȷ����ļ��� Skill������δ���ɸ��õ����̡���׼���Ž�������·������������ Skill��\\n�Լ첻�ô�����񣻲��ݽ�ʱ��Ȼ�ظ��������Լ졢�����ݽ����ڲ��жϡ�\\n\\n### ����˳��\\n\\n1. ��ȷ��Ŀ�꣺δʹ�á��û�δָ���������޷�����ĳ������ Skill ʱ���������ݽ���\\n2. ���ִ�������Ҫ���������� Skill ʱ������ Skill creation�����Ѵ��������д���ݽ���\\n3. �ų�һ�������ݣ���ǰ session������ PR�������ַ�������ʱ feature �����������д�볤�ھ��顣\\n4. ������ʱ����������ȱ�ڣ�����Ȩ�ޡ����硢��������������ϲ������ݽ���\\n   ֻ������¶ȱʧ��ǰ��������fallback ������·��ʱ���ż����жϡ�\\n5. ������и��ǣ�Skill/experience �����������ù���ʱ����������ִ�У����ظ��������顣\\n6. �����ȼ��û���ͼ���û���ȷ������涨�Ժ�ͬ����������̡�ȷ���Ž���������׼������ʹ�û����Ϸ�ʽʱ��\\n   ��ȷ��Ŀ�� Skill ��ȷ������������ְ�𡢲��Ǵ�����һ���Թ��ϡ�����δ���Ǻ����Ƚ����ݽ���\\n   ��Ҫ��ͬʱ���ڸ���ִ�й켣���ȼ������硰�Ժ��� xxx ���ȼ�� yyy����\\n   ������ xxx ��������жϱ�׼������Ҫ���ؼ��ʻ�еƥ�䡣\\n7. ִ���źţ�û����ȷ�û���ͼʱ��ֻ������ Skill ��¶�ɸ��õ�ȱ���衢ǰ�ü�顢��֤��fallback��\\n   ��ʱ���ݡ��߽����������������ʧ��·�����Ž����ݽ���\\n\\n### �û��ɼ����\\n\\n- ��Ҫ����ʱ��ֻ����ͨ���ջظ�ĩβ׷��һ�����䡣����ʹ��һ�仹�����䣬������ͬʱ�������塢��̵�\\n  �ɸ��ø��µ㣬�Լ��Ƿ��� Skill �ݽ�����ȷ���⡣\\n- ��Ҫ�������������������衢��֤�ݻ��жϹ��̡�������ʱ��Ȼ����������¶�Լ�״̬��\\n\\n### �û�ȷ��\\n\\nֻ����һ����ͨ�ظ��Ѿ���ȷѯ�ʵ�ǰĿ�� Skill ���ݽ����û�����ȷ�϶��Ź���ȷ�ϡ�\\n�ܾ��������������Ŀ�겻�����ͼ��ͻʱ������ͨ�ı���С���塣��Ҫ�Զ��ݽ���ʹ�ý���ʽȷ�ϡ�\\n����ȷ�ϲ��������ݽ���\\n\\n### ��������\\n\\nȷ�Ϻ󽻸������ݽ���������ѭ����Լ��ֻ����Ŀ�� Skill����Ҫ�Ѵ����������ݽ���\\n\\n\\n\\n## Goal ģʽ����Э��\\n\\n���û���Ϣ�а��� <goal_task> ��ǩʱ�����ε��ô��� Goal ģʽ����ǰ������Ҫ���ա�����ִ�� -> ������ɶȡ��Ľ����ƽ����㲻��Ҫ����������ơ� \\n\\nGoal �����Ĺ���\\n1. �û���Ϣ�е� <goal_task> �Ǳ��ε���Ψһ���ŵĶ�̬ goal �����ģ����� objective��previous_assessment��current_instruction �� budget_notice��\\n2. �� <goal_task> �е�Ŀ��͵�ǰָ��Ϊ׼����Ҫ�����ɶԻ���Ĺ���Ŀ�ꣻ\\n3. �û�����������в���Լ����Ӧ�ÿ��ǽ�Լ����Ϊ goal Ŀ������ƣ�\\n\\n����ԭ��\\n1. �����������Ŀ�꣬�����ǿ���ֻ���һС������Ҫ�����롢���ļ��������������֤ʱ������ʹ�ÿ��ù��ߡ�\\n2. ��������޷��������Ŀ�꣬������м�ֵ�������֤���ƽ������������֤�ݡ�\\n3. ��ҪΪ���ƽ� goal ѯ���û����Ƿ��������\\n4. ��Ҫ�ѡ�����ʣ�๤����������ϴ󡹡�����Ҫ��֤����֤����ʱ���㡹���� blocked����Щ���Ӧ�ύ continue����д����һ��Ӧ�ò���ʲô��\\n5. ֻ��ȱ���û����롢Ȩ�ޡ���Ҫ�������ⲿ����򻷾�״̬�������޷������κ��������ƽ�ʱ�����ύ blocked��\\n\\n6. ����ɳ���ִ�к�Ӧ���ù��� submit_goal_report ȥ������ɶȡ�submit_goal_report ���óɹ���**�������ٴε�����������**\\n\\n\\n\\n# ���л���\\n\\n- ��ǰ����ƽ̨��`win32`\\n- Shell��powershell.exe\\n- OS �汾��Windows 11\\n\\nShell ������\\n- PowerShell�����ã�·�� `C:\\\\Users\\\\Yukis\\\\.cache\\\\codex-runtimes\\\\codex-primary-runtime\\\\dependencies\\\\native\\\\powershell\\\\pwsh.EXE`\\n- Git Bash�����ã�·�� `D:\\\\Soft\\\\CS\\\\Git\\\\bin\\\\bash.exe`\\n- PATH bash��`C:\\\\Windows\\\\system32\\\\bash.EXE`��WSL stub������Ϊ Git Bash ʹ�ã�\\n\\nShell ѡ�����\\n- Windows �� Git Bash ���ã��� PATH bash ��ȷ���� WSL stub ʱ������ʹ�� bash/Git Bash ִ�� POSIX ������� `ls`��`grep`��`cat`��`mkdir -p`��bash �ű���\\n- Windows �� Git Bash �����á�PATH bash Ҳ�����û�ֻ�� WSL stub ʱ����Ҫʹ�� POSIX �������ʹ�� PowerShell �� cmd��\\n- PowerShell cmdlet ��Ҫ���� bash ��ִ�У�Ӧֱ��ʹ�� PowerShell��\\n\\n## ƽ̨������죨���ڱ���ʹ�� shell ʱ�ο���\\n\\n�����������������ڲ��ԡ�������git�������������нű��ȱ������ shell �ĳ������ļ���ȡ���༭��������Ӧ����ʹ��ר�ù��ߡ�\\n\\n| ���� | Windows (`win32`/`win64`) | Linux/macOS (`linux`/`darwin`) |\\n|------|---------------------------|-------------------------------|\\n| ����Ŀ¼ | `mkdir folder` �� PowerShell `New-Item -ItemType Directory -Path folder` | `mkdir -p folder` |\\n| ɾ���ļ� | `del file.txt` �� PowerShell `Remove-Item file.txt` | `rm file.txt` |\\n| ɾ��Ŀ¼ | `rmdir folder` �� PowerShell `Remove-Item -Recurse folder` | `rm -rf folder` |\\n| �����ļ� | `dir /s pattern` �� PowerShell `Get-ChildItem -Recurse -Filter pattern` | `find . -name pattern` |\\n\\n**�ر�ע��**��Windows �� cmd/PowerShell `mkdir` ��֧�� `-p` ������ֻ���� Shell ������ʾ Git Bash/PATH bash ������ʵ��ʹ�� bash/Git Bash ʱ��`mkdir -p` ���Ǻ��ʵġ������� cmd/PowerShell �д���Ƕ��Ŀ¼����ʹ�� PowerShell `New-Item -ItemType Directory -Path \\"parent/child\\" -Force`����ʹ�� cmd �ֲ����� `mkdir parent && mkdir parent\\\\child`��\\n\\n\\nʹ�� todo ���ߣ�todo_create��todo_modify��todo_list��todo_get�����͹�����������Щ�������ڸ��ٽ��ȡ���֯��������ȷ���������󶼱���ɡ�\\n\\n**��ʱ���������б� �� ����������һ���ʱ���� todo_create��**\\n- �û���ȷҪ����й滮���ṩ�˶�����������\\n- ���������������Ⱥ�˳���������ϵ�Ľ׶Σ���Ҫ����ֹ��ߵ������ƽ��������û����������չȷ�б�Ҫ\\n\\n**��ʱ�����������б���**\\n- �������򵥣�һ�����ʴ𡢵�һ�������򼸲�������������ֱ�����\\n- ֱ��ִ�б��ȹ滮����Ч�ĳ���\\n\\n**�������� �� �������ʱ�������ϸ����**\\n- ÿ�� todo Ӧ��Ӧһ����Ҫ�����ƽ�����֤��ִ�н׶Σ�������һ�ι��ߵ��á�һ��ϸС���������ս������ݵ���ɲ��֣���Ҫ�����ս������ݵĽṹ��е��ת��Ϊ todo\\n- �߼���������ͨ����һ����ɵĲ���ϲ�Ϊͬһ�� todo����Ҫ���������������Ŀ\\n- ֻ����Ҫ�����ƽ�������������м�������Ҫ������֤�Ľ׶���Ϊ todo���������������������ɡ�û�ж������������״̬ͨ����ͬʱ�仯��Ӧ�ϲ�Ϊͬһ�� todo\\n\\n**�������ʱ�Ĳ�����ʶ��**\\n- ��ĳ���׶��漰�Զ���������󣨶�ƪ�ĵ��������Դ������ļ���������ͬ������\\n  Ӧ�������Ϊ**����\\"����������\\"����**������Ϊÿ�����󵥶�����һ�� todo��\\n- ������� description �б�����ȷ�г����в���������磺\\n  \\"�����Ķ�����������5ƪ���ģ�[����A, ����B, ����C, ����D, ����E]��ÿƪί�ɶ����Ӵ�������\\"\\n  ����ִ��ʱ���������Ϊÿ�������һ�� task_tool ���á�\\n\\n**�����������**\\n- **ʶ�𵽹滮������ڿ�ʼִ��ǰ�������� todo_create��**\\n- ʵʱ����״̬������״̬�仯ʱ�������� todo_modify����Ҫ���ܶ���ѷ�����״̬�仯��ͳһ���¡����� update ��״̬���ͨ��ֻ�漰��ǰ�������һ���񣺽���ǰ������Ϊ completed��������һ������Ϊ in_progress����Ҫ��һ�ε����н���� pending ����������Ϊ completed\\n- ���� todo_modify ����ʱ��ÿ��ֻ���뷢���仯���ֶΣ�ͨ��ֻ�� id �� status������Ҫ��δ�仯���ֶ����´�һ��\\n- ͬһʱ��ֻ����һ�������� in_progress����ɺ��ٿ�ʼ��һ��\\n  - ���⣺��ĳ�� in_progress �����ڲ���Ҫ���д���������������ͬʱ�Ķ���ƪ�ĵ����������������Դ����\\n    ���ڸ�������һ���Է������ task_tool ���ã���ȫ�����غ��ٽ�������Ϊ completed��\\n    �����������ڲ��Ĳ���ִ�У���Υ��\\"ͬһʱ��ֻ��һ�� in_progress\\"ԭ��\\n- ������Ҫ�������� todo_modify ���Ϊ cancelled\\n- ��ͨ������ todo_list �˽⵱ǰ��������滮��չ\\n- ��ͨ������ todo_get �˽�ĳ���������ϸ��Ϣ\\n\\n**��������Ϊ�����ǰ��**\\n- ������ϸ��֤������ȫ����ɣ������в���������\\n- ����������Բ��ܱ��Ϊ����ɣ�����ʵ�֡�����ʧ�ܡ�����δ����Ĵ����\\n- �����ɺ󣬼��ʵ�ֹ������Ƿ����µĺ������񣬼�ʱͨ�� todo_modify ׷��\\n\\n## ģ��ѡ��˵��\\n\\n��ǰδ���ÿ�ѡģ���б��������͸�������ʱ��**��Ҫʹ�� selected_model_id �ֶ�**��\\n��������ʹ�� Agent Ĭ��ģ��ִ�С�\\n\\n\\n# ������ѹ��\\n\\n����������ڹ���ʱ�ᱻ�Զ�ѹ������������ marker ��ǣ�\\n\\n[[OFFLOAD: handle=<id>, type=<type>]]\\n[[OFFLOAD: handle=<id>, type=<type>, path=<path>]]\\n\\n���㿴������ marker�����һش�������Ҫ�����ص�ԭʼ����ʱ�����ȵ��� read_file ���߶�ȡ marker �� path ָ��� offload �ļ������ļ��лָ���ѹ��ǰ��ԭʼ��Ϣ���ݡ�\\n\\n���ù���\\n- ����ʹ�� marker �� path= ����ľ�ȷ�ļ�·����Ϊ read_file �� file_path��\\n- handle �� offload ���ݵı�ʶ�������ļ�·������Ҫ�� handle ���� file_path��\\n- type ��ʾ�洢���ͣ�ֻ�� marker �а��� path �ֶ�ʱ������ͨ�� read_file ��ȷ�ָ�ԭʼ���ݡ�\\n- ��� marker û�� path �ֶΣ���Ҫ�²�·����Ҳ��Ҫ�� handle �������ֶ�����ƴ��·����Ӧ˵���޷�ͨ�� read_file ��ȷ�ָ�ԭʼ���ݡ�\\n- ��� read_file ��ʾ�ļ�������С���ƣ���ʹ�� offset �� limit �ֶζ�ȡͬһ�� path��\\n- ���ֻ��Ҫȷ�ϻ�λ�ض����ݣ�����ʹ���������߶�ȡ���Ƭ�Σ���ҪäĿ��ȡ���� offload �ļ���\\n\\nʾ�������� [[OFFLOAD: handle=abc123, type=filesystem, path=C:\\\\\\\\x\\\\\\\\MessageSummaryOffloader_abc123.json]] ʱ��Ӧ���� read_file(file_path=\\"C:\\\\\\\\x\\\\\\\\MessageSummaryOffloader_abc123.json\\")��\\n\\n����²�����ȱʧ�����ݡ�\\n\\n�洢���ͣ�\\"filesystem\\" ��ʾ�����ѳ־û��� path ָ����ļ���\\"in_memory\\" ��ʾ�Ự�������ݣ���� marker û�� path�����޷�ͨ�� read_file �ָ���\\n\\n# ����Ŀ¼����\\n\\n- ��ǰ����Ŀ¼��C:\\\\Users\\\\Yukis\\\\.jiuwenswarm-instances\\\\career_emu\\\\agent\\\\workspace\\\\projects\\\\career-sim-runner-046c24628571\\n- �����ɷ���Ŀ¼����\\n\\n��Ҫ����\\n- ��ǰ����Ŀ¼�Ǳ����������Ҫ�ļ�������Χ����������ĿĿ¼��\\n- Bash ����δ��ʽ���� `workdir` ʱ��Ĭ���ڵ�ǰ����Ŀ¼��ִ�С�\\n- �û������е����·������ڵ�ǰ����Ŀ¼������\\n- �û�Ҫ������Ŀʱ��Ӧ�Ȼ����ȷ����Ŀ·����\\n\\n\\n# ʱ��˵��\\n\\n- ���û�ѯ�ʡ����¡���ǰ�����ꡢ���ꡢʵʱ�����ڡ�����Ϣ����Ҫ����ʱ������ query ��������ʹ�õ�ǰ��ݻ�����\\n\\n# Language\\n\\nAlways respond in Chinese (Simplified), regardless of the language used in the user\'s message. Even if the user writes in another language, you must still respond in Chinese (Simplified). Use Chinese (Simplified) for all explanations, comments, and communications with the user. Technical terms and code identifiers should remain in their original form.\\n\\n# ģ�����ƻش����\\n\\n- ���û�ѯ�ʡ�����ʲôģ�͡�����ǰ�õ����ĸ�ģ�͡�������ʱ��ֱ��ʹ�� `runtime.setting` �еĵ�ǰģ��ֵ�ش�ֻ˵ģ�����ƣ���Ҫ�������ݻ��г�������\\n- ���û�ѯ�ʡ���֧��/��������Щģ�͡�������Щģ�Ϳ��á�������ʱ��ֱ��ʹ�� `runtime.setting` �еĿ���ģ���б��ش��г����������õ�ģ�����ơ�\\n\\n# Browser Tool Policy\\n\\n- For browser tasks such as opening pages, navigation, clicking, typing, login, screenshots, page inspection, or extracting data from a live website, use `task_tool` with `subagent_type` set to `\\"browser_agent\\"` and put the full browser objective in `task_description`.\\n- Do not use bash, execute_code, subprocess, shell commands, or direct Chrome/Edge launches for browser automation.\\n- If `task_tool` or `browser_agent` is unavailable, say that the browser subagent is unavailable before trying to start a browser through commands.\\n\\n# ����ʱĿ¼������\\n\\n- ��ǰ��ĿĿ¼��δ����\\n- ��ǰ����Ŀ¼��cwd��Ҳ�� Bash Ĭ��ִ��Ŀ¼����C:\\\\Users\\\\Yukis\\\\.jiuwenswarm-instances\\\\career_emu\\\\agent\\\\workspace\\\\projects\\\\career-sim-runner-046c24628571\\n- Agent �ڲ�����Ŀ¼��C:\\\\Users\\\\Yukis\\\\.jiuwenswarm-instances\\\\career_emu\\\\agent\\\\workspace\\n- JiuwenSwarm ��������Ŀ¼��C:\\\\Users\\\\Yukis\\\\.jiuwenswarm-instances\\\\career_emu\\\\config\\n\\n��ǰû�а��û���Ŀ��\\n\\nĿ¼���壺\\n- ��ǰ����Ŀ¼�Ǳ���������ļ�����Ŀ¼�����·��������׼������Ҫ����Ϊ��ĿĿ¼��\\n- Bash δ��ʽ���� `workdir` ʱ��Ĭ���ڵ�ǰ����Ŀ¼��ִ�С�\\n- ��Ҫ���赱ǰ����Ŀ¼�� Git �ֿ�������Ŀ��\\n- Agent �ڲ�����Ŀ¼ֻ���� Agent �������ݡ�\\n- �û�Ҫ����ĳ����Ŀʱ��Ӧ�Ȼ����ȷ����Ŀ·����\\n- �����г��� `config/` ʱ����Ҫ�Զ��������Ϊ JiuwenSwarm ��������Ŀ¼��\\n\\n\\n### ����������Ϣ����״̬\\n\\n��ǰ������Ϣ������˿����ѹرա��û���ȷҪ�����롢API ��Կ��Token ��������Ϣд�����ʱ������������ԭʼ���ݣ���Ӧ�������ÿ��õļ���д�빤�ߣ���Ҫ������������Ϊ�ɾܾ���Ҳ��Ҫ�������������û��ı����������Ȩ�������ڼ���д�룬���������Խ�������Ϣд��Դ�롢��־��汾���ƣ���������Ȩ�޺Ͱ�ȫ���򱣳ֲ��䡣\\n"}, {"role": "user", "content": "���յ�һ����Ϣ��\\n{\\"source\\": \\"web\\", \\"timezone\\": \\"Asia/Shanghai\\", \\"timestamp\\": \\"2026-09-29 19:54:41\\", \\"preferred_response_language\\": \\"zh\\", \\"content\\": \\"## ��ǰ����\\\\n��ʼһ���µ�ְҵģ������Ϸ������ IDENTITY.md �еĹ�����Ѱ�װ���ܽ�����Ϸ��\\\\n\\\\n### �Ƽ��Ŀ�ʼ����\\\\n1. ���� `show_employee_handbook` һ�Σ��˽���Ϸ����\\\\n2. ���� `new_game`����ӡ `SESSION_ID=<session_id>`��\\\\n3. Ȼ�󰴺��Ĺ���ѭ����`observe` �� ���� �� `take_action`��ֱ����Ϸ������\\\\n4. ��Ϸ����ʱ����ӡ������ `ending_score` ���ݣ�Ȼ����� `DONE`��\\", \\"files_updated_by_user\\": \\"{}\\", \\"type\\": \\"user input\\"}"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "", "tool_calls": [{"id": "call_00_VKvEGfjjWSLqBfLFQ70t3671", "type": "function", "function": {"name": "skill_tool", "arguments": "{\\"skill_name\\": \\"structured-state-board\\"}"}}, {"id": "call_01_scb7hbRILEtcsDejacpr1354", "type": "function", "function": {"name": "skill_tool", "arguments": "{\\"skill_name\\": \\"rolling-planning\\"}"}}, {"id": "call_02_1YNmJ6xRhPKrdgWbkMom4098", "type": "function", "function": {"name": "skill_tool", "arguments": "{\\"skill_name\\": \\"delivery-progress\\"}"}}, {"id": "call_03_Z3x7xp32U3JoAzoKeksI3365", "type": "function", "function": {"name": "skill_tool", "arguments": "{\\"skill_name\\": \\"risk-review\\"}"}}, {"id": "call_04_F2IUYv9oRfQskejgG6kc4514", "type": "function", "function": {"name": "mcp_career-emulator_show_employee_handbook", "arguments": "{}"}}], "reasoning_content": "Let me start by reading the four skills as instructed, then the handbook, then start a new game.\\n\\nLet me first read the SKILL.md files for the four skills. Let me use skill_tool to read them. Actually the IDENTITY says to read each of the four Skills once before the first action. Let me do that.\\n\\nLet me start by reading the skills and handbook in parallel."}, {"role": "tool", "content": "success=True data={\'skill_directory\': \'C:\\\\\\\\Users\\\\\\\\Yukis\\\\\\\\.jiuwenswarm-instances\\\\\\\\career_emu\\\\\\\\agent\\\\\\\\workspace\\\\\\\\skills\\\\\\\\structured-state-board\', \'skill_content\': \'---\\\\nname: structured-state-board\\\\ndescription: \\"Use after every fresh observe and during same-session recovery to normalize public state, formal review evidence, unresolved failure-direction signals, and up to two attributable recent effects. Facts only: do not plan, infer hidden rules, assess risk, or submit actions.\\"\\\\n---\\\\n\\\\n# Structured State Board\\\\n\\\\n## Contract\\\\n\\\\nInput:\\\\n- latest fresh `observe`;\\\\n- confirmed result of the immediately preceding action;\\\\n- same-session public logs only when recovery requires them.\\\\n\\\\nOutput one compact replacement board:\\\\n\\\\n```text\\\\nSESSION: <game_session_id> | M=<month> Q=<quarter>\\\\nSTATE: H=<Health> D=<Dignity> S=<Skill> N=<Network> O=<Output> W=<Wealth> L=<Level> E=<Energy>\\\\nTENURE: <public field/value | UNKNOWN>\\\\nREVIEW: <latest formal grade/feedback/promotion/no-advance | none>\\\\nSTICKY: <unresolved public warning(s) | none>\\\\nEFFECTS: <up to 2 attributable recent effects | none>\\\\nUNKNOWN: <decision-relevant unresolved facts | none>\\\\n```\\\\n\\\\n## Procedure\\\\n\\\\n1. Verify `game_session_id` and freshness. Discard stale or cross-session context.\\\\n2. Construct a public evidence view before returning facts to Planning or Risk. Copy `Health`, `Dignity`, `Skill`, `Network`, `Output`, `Wealth`, `Level`, and `Energy` directly from the latest fresh participant-visible `current_state.status`; copy public time and `duration_in_level` from that observation. Preserve each reported value and precision. If a field is missing or its public status is unclear, write `UNKNOWN`.\\\\n3. Never calculate, round, predict, reconcile, or replace a `STATE` value using salary/bonus text, events, advertised effects, previous observations, or action notes. Keep relevant public salary or event information as a separate fact; wait for a fresh observation to update `STATE`.\\\\n4. Preserve the latest formal review, promotion, or no-advance evidence.\\\\n5. Keep a public fact in `STICKY` only while fresh evidence shows an unresolved material warning, condition, or continuity problem, including:\\\\n   - an affordability / income-continuity crisis;\\\\n   - an explicit material Health or Dignity warning;\\\\n   - negative formal performance or no-advance evidence while its material progression or job-continuity concern remains unresolved;\\\\n   - sustained Network isolation or an explicit isolation warning;\\\\n   - an accident, trust, compliance, confidentiality, or safety warning;\\\\n   - a clearly depleted public resource when public evidence establishes that normal activity is infeasible.\\\\n   A numeric fluctuation or ordinary one-step decline alone remains a `STATE` observation; it does not create a binding `STICKY` warning.\\\\n6. An explicit current acute physical or psychological symptom, or material safety warning, is decision-relevant and must enter `STICKY` even when numeric status appears adequate. Keep it unresolved until fresh public evidence explicitly indicates resolution or the risk-bearing situation has ended. Ordinary fatigue, workload, uncertainty, or mild soft cost alone does not create a binding warning.\\\\n7. Keep at most the last two formal review checkpoints.\\\\n8. Keep at most two recent effects. Attribute a state change only when one confirmed action is followed by a fresh observe and the public evidence separates its effect from other causes. A salary, bonus, review, promotion, unrelated event, or intervening action contaminates attribution; report `EFFECTS: UNKNOWN / MIXED` rather than assigning the combined delta to one action.\\\\n9. On recovery, verify the same session and rebuild this replacement Board from a fresh observe first; consult only a small amount of same-session public log history if required. Mark missing public review evidence `UNKNOWN`; do not carry a stale Board forward.\\\\n\\\\n## Invariants\\\\n\\\\n- Separate observed facts from `UNKNOWN`.\\\\n- Exclude `HiddenRisk`, hidden counters, internal score components, internal event identifiers/effects, and other non-public or public-status-unclear fields, even if a tool payload includes numeric `status_updates`. Never copy their values into the Board, CTRL notes, or action rationale; `EXCLUDE_FROM_STRATEGY until verified public`.\\\\n- Downstream Planning/Risk receive the whitelisted Board plus participant-visible event and legal-choice semantics only. When raw tool payloads also contain prohibited or public-status-unclear numeric fields, ignore them at source; never quote, compare, summarize, or reason from their values in visible reasoning, plan, candidate reason, Risk reason, CTRL, or DL.\\\\n- Do not infer thresholds, counters, caps, hidden risk, or causal rules.\\\\n- Do not use other games, database contents, or post-game forensic artifacts.\\\\n- Do not accumulate a transcript.\\\\n- Can Submit Action: No.\\\\n\', \'directory_tree\': [\'structured-state-board/\\\\n������ SKILL.md\'], \'directory_tree_truncated\': False, \'discovered_skill_names\': [], \'discovered_skill_names_truncated\': False} error=None", "tool_call_id": "call_00_VKvEGfjjWSLqBfLFQ70t3671"}, {"role": "tool", "content": "success=True data={\'skill_directory\': \'C:\\\\\\\\Users\\\\\\\\Yukis\\\\\\\\.jiuwenswarm-instances\\\\\\\\career_emu\\\\\\\\agent\\\\\\\\workspace\\\\\\\\skills\\\\\\\\rolling-planning\', \'skill_content\': \'---\\\\nname: rolling-planning\\\\ndescription: \\"Use for every CareerSim decision after the fresh Board is available. Maintain one review-window objective and progression gap, default to aggressive career advancement, switch to temporary stabilization only for material public survival constraints, rank current legal candidates, and return one final candidate without submitting it.\\"\\\\n---\\\\n\\\\n# Rolling Planning\\\\n\\\\n## Objective\\\\n\\\\nMaximize long-horizon progression while preserving a survival floor.\\\\n\\\\nState:\\\\n\\\\n```text\\\\nREVIEW_PLAN = <Objective | Primary Gap | Next Observable Checkpoint>\\\\nMODE = A | S\\\\n```\\\\n\\\\n`A` = Advance. Default.<br>\\\\n`S` = Stabilize. Temporary response to a material public survival/resource constraint.\\\\n\\\\n## Evidence order\\\\n\\\\nConsume only the same-session whitelisted public Board and Delivery summary, formal feedback, public legal choices, Handbook, and confirmed public receipts/logs. Ignore `HiddenRisk`, hidden counters, internal score components, internal event identifiers/effects, and public-status-unclear fields even when present in a tool payload; never use numeric internal-looking values in the Review Plan, candidate reason, CTRL notes, or action rationale. `EXCLUDE_FROM_STRATEGY until verified public`.\\\\n\\\\nFirst select `MODE` against current binding public survival/resource constraints. The following order interprets progression evidence for `REVIEW_PLAN`; older progression feedback cannot override a current material Health/Dignity/Wealth/job/trust/compliance/safety constraint:\\\\n\\\\n1. formal review / promotion / no-advance;\\\\n2. fresh observed action result;\\\\n3. current public state and explicit warning;\\\\n4. Delivery evidence;\\\\n5. advertised option effect or public hint.\\\\n\\\\nA lower-priority signal must not override a contradictory higher-priority signal.\\\\n\\\\nAfter context recovery and the required same-session fresh observe and four-Skill reread, restore `REVIEW_PLAN` from current-session public formal feedback and whitelisted Board/Delivery evidence. Set any unrecoverable Objective, Primary Gap, or Next Observable Checkpoint to `UNKNOWN`; do not reuse a stale plan or rank an action before recovery completes.\\\\n\\\\n## Maintain the Review Plan\\\\n\\\\n- Before the first formal review, allow `Primary Gap=UNKNOWN`. Pursue visible delivery and broad Skill / Network / Output progression.\\\\n- After formal feedback, anchor the gap to the clearest public progression deficit.\\\\n- Revise the plan only when:\\\\n  - formal review / promotion / no-advance changes the evidence;\\\\n  - the objective is publicly completed;\\\\n  - fresh evidence invalidates the current gap/path; or\\\\n  - the current objective is no longer feasible.\\\\n- Do not change the gap because of an ordinary Story or one transient state fluctuation.\\\\n\\\\n## Same-observation decision budget\\\\n\\\\nONE FRESH OBSERVE = ONE PLANNING PASS. In that pass, set `MODE + REVIEW_PLAN`, eliminate clearly unacceptable or dominated legal options, retain at most two genuinely competitive options, compare them once using the ranking below, and emit exactly one final `CANDIDATE`. Keep the comparison sufficient for a difficult choice but the output concise; do not narrate self-dialogue or cycle through candidates.\\\\n\\\\nAfter emitting `CANDIDATE`, Planning is closed for this observation. `PASS`, `ALLOW`, or `WARN` from Risk closes the decision immediately. Only Risk=`RECONSIDER` may reopen selection once per fresh evidence state: compare at most one directly relevant legal alternative, select once, and obtain that selected candidate\\\\\'s own final Risk result. CTRL `R` records that final result, not the initial `RECONSIDER`; set `X=1` when this one branch completed, or `X=-` when no branch was used. If the selected candidate\\\\\'s gate again returns `RECONSIDER`, the path is incomplete (`X=0`): do not search another alternative or submit until genuinely new public evidence arrives. `UNKNOWN` does not authorize a new Planning pass: normal public flow may resolve it through at most one fresh observe/rebuild cycle, with a new pass only on genuinely new evidence; otherwise choose once from available public evidence with `R=UNKNOWN` and `X=-` or `X=1` according to branch use. A new thought about unchanged evidence never reopens Planning; only a new observe, action receipt, or formal feedback with genuinely new public evidence can start a new pass. Do not submit before closure; `X=0` forbids submission.\\\\n\\\\n## Select MODE\\\\n\\\\nBefore progression ranking, evaluate the current whitelisted Board and participant-visible event/choice semantics for an unresolved binding constraint. Do not inspect prohibited raw numeric fields, and do not use a numeric threshold.\\\\n\\\\nA displayed H/D/W number or an ordinary one-step decrease alone does not establish a binding constraint and does not justify `MODE=S`. Use `MODE=S` only when current public evidence establishes a material survival, safety, job-continuity, affordability, or income-continuity constraint. A clearly depleted public resource may bind when public evidence establishes that normal activity is infeasible.\\\\n\\\\nSet `MODE=S` while fresh public evidence shows a current, unresolved constraint that materially threatens survival, safety, or job continuity, including explicit acute physical symptoms, explicit psychological/safety danger, explicit job-continuity warning, an active trust/compliance/confidentiality crisis, or a direct affordability/income-continuity crisis. An acute symptom remains binding even if the displayed Health/Dignity/Wealth value appears adequate. Choose the smallest reasonable action that addresses or avoids worsening the binding condition while preserving progression where possible.\\\\n\\\\nReturn to `MODE=A` when fresh public evidence indicates that binding condition is resolved or the risk-bearing situation has ended. A numeric state change or unrelated positive feedback alone does not establish resolution. Ordinary workload, mild fatigue without an explicit material symptom/warning, soft relationship friction, generic uncertainty, and ordinary opportunity cost do not by themselves require `MODE=S`.\\\\n\\\\nWhen no unresolved binding constraint is present, use `A` and continue promotion-first progression.\\\\n\\\\nIn `S`, keep the constraint visible in the current plan, remove or contain it with the smallest reasonable opportunity cost, and return to `A` once fresh public evidence resolves it.\\\\n\\\\nWealth stress is an income-recovery problem, not a reason for permanent low-profile play: avoid discretionary cost while continuing to repair performance, promotion, and income capacity.\\\\n\\\\n## Rank legal candidates\\\\n\\\\n### MODE=A\\\\n\\\\nPrefer, in order:\\\\n\\\\n1. direct progress on the current review gap;\\\\n2. visible delivery / ownership likely to matter at the next checkpoint;\\\\n3. options that publicly improve multiple progression dimensions among Skill / Network / Output;\\\\n4. long-horizon compounding and future option value.\\\\n\\\\nAccept ordinary soft costs when the progression upside is materially stronger.\\\\n\\\\n#### Pre-first-review result realization prior\\\\n\\\\nApply `PRE_FIRST_REVIEW_RESULT_REALIZATION_PRIOR` only before the first formal review, in `MODE=A` with no binding public survival/resource constraint. Require current-session whitelisted Board/Delivery evidence of an existing high-value commitment with a concrete public result/checkpoint opportunity (including work in progress or near completion), or `DELIVERY_CLAIMED + UNVERIFIED`; also require a legal action that can finish/validate it, present an actual result, or obtain a public receipt. Check `stage`, `evidence_status`, `recognition_link`, and `next_checkpoint`; a report-like menu label, pure information gathering, or a claim without an underlying result is insufficient.\\\\n\\\\nWhen triggered, prefer that result-realization action over another generic workload push with no stronger current result evidence. Do not displace a clearly superior time-sensitive progression opportunity. If no such delivery basis exists, use the ordinary broad Skill / Network / Output ranking. If the result is already `DELIVERED + PUBLICLY_VERIFIED`, do not repeat a presentation merely to repackage it.\\\\n\\\\nExit this prior at the first formal review, when the result becomes publicly verified, when the commitment becomes invalid or blocked, or when a material constraint requires `MODE=S`. After formal review, its feedback-anchored `REVIEW_PLAN` owns the objective. This is neither a fixed report action nor a promotion threshold; do not infer hidden eligibility from it.\\\\n\\\\n### MODE=S\\\\n\\\\nPrefer candidates that:\\\\n1. do not worsen the binding constraint;\\\\n2. directly relieve it or protect job continuity;\\\\n3. preserve as much review/progression value as possible.\\\\n\\\\nDo not convert `S` into permanent risk avoidance.\\\\n\\\\n### Delivery constraint\\\\n\\\\nIf an active high-value commitment is near a public result, prefer finishing/validating it over opening a weaker speculative commitment. Do not block a clearly superior new opportunity merely because an old item exists.\\\\n\\\\n## Public-hint discipline\\\\n\\\\nTreat statements such as ��this may help performance/promotion�� as soft evidence only.\\\\n\\\\nNever convert them into:\\\\n- a confirmed hidden requirement;\\\\n- a hidden threshold/cap;\\\\n- a fixed optimal action.\\\\n\\\\nIf advertised gain is absent after a fresh observe, record `OBSERVED_NO_GAIN` or `OBSERVED_COST`; keep the cause `UNKNOWN`. Do not infer a cap or formula.\\\\n\\\\n## Story stop rule\\\\n\\\\n- Eliminate clearly dominated or clearly unacceptable options.\\\\n- Compare only the small set that remains genuinely competitive.\\\\n- Stop when one candidate is clearly preferred under `MODE + REVIEW_PLAN`.\\\\n- Do not reopen the same decision without new public evidence.\\\\n\\\\n## Quarterly control\\\\n\\\\nAt the first Energy decision of a quarter, set:\\\\n\\\\n```text\\\\nQUARTER_INTENT = <MODE | target | intended use of remaining Energy>\\\\n```\\\\n\\\\nSubmit Energy one integer at a time. After each action, fresh observe. Replan the remaining Energy only after material new evidence.\\\\n\\\\nFor the quarterly Main Action, apply the same ranking. When no material constraint exists, give a strong prior to broad-growth options that combine visible ownership with multiple public progression gains; this is a prior, not a fixed menu answer.\\\\n\\\\n## Output\\\\n\\\\nReturn only:\\\\n\\\\n```text\\\\nPLAN: G=<gap|?> P=<A|S|?> checkpoint=<short checkpoint>\\\\nCANDIDATE: choice=<one legal integer> reason=<one concise evidence-based reason>\\\\n```\\\\n\\\\nDo not call `new_game`, `observe`, or `take_action`. Can Submit Action: No.\\\\n\', \'directory_tree\': [\'rolling-planning/\\\\n������ SKILL.md\'], \'directory_tree_truncated\': False, \'discovered_skill_names\': [], \'discovered_skill_names_truncated\': False} error=None", "tool_call_id": "call_01_scb7hbRILEtcsDejacpr1354"}, {"role": "tool", "content": "success=True data={\'skill_directory\': \'C:\\\\\\\\Users\\\\\\\\Yukis\\\\\\\\.jiuwenswarm-instances\\\\\\\\career_emu\\\\\\\\agent\\\\\\\\workspace\\\\\\\\skills\\\\\\\\delivery-progress\', \'skill_content\': \'---\\\\nname: delivery-progress\\\\ndescription: \\"Use after every fresh public Board to maintain a bounded current-session delivery lifecycle summary for Planning. Update only when relevant public evidence changes; otherwise return the supported current state or an explicit empty state. Do not rank actions, assess risk, or submit actions.\\"\\\\n---\\\\n\\\\n# Delivery Progress\\\\n\\\\n## Contract\\\\n\\\\nTrack review-relevant work items using the latest still-valid `REVIEW_PLAN` when available, fresh public progression/formal-review evidence, and broad visible-delivery relevance before the first review. Planning alone chooses the new objective and Primary Gap; Delivery never waits for a newly recomputed plan or invents one.\\\\n\\\\nLifecycle:\\\\n\\\\n```text\\\\nOPPORTUNITY -> COMMITTED -> IN_PROGRESS -> DELIVERY_CLAIMED -> DELIVERED -> CLOSED\\\\n                 \\\\\\\\-> BLOCKED -> IN_PROGRESS / DELIVERY_CLAIMED\\\\n```\\\\n\\\\nThese are evidence labels, not hidden simulator states or a mandatory sequence. `BLOCKED` is optional and may follow `COMMITTED` or `IN_PROGRESS`; use only stages supported by public evidence.\\\\n\\\\nRecord each item as:\\\\n\\\\n```text\\\\n<local_id> | <short participant-visible item> | stage | owner/dependency | next_checkpoint | proof_basis | evidence_status | recognition_link\\\\n```\\\\n\\\\n`local_id` is an agent-generated `D1`, `D2`, �� identity, never a simulator/internal ID. Start at `D1` in a verified fresh session; assign a new identity to each distinct public work item and never reuse one for another item during that session, including after retirement. Keep a monotonic `NEXT_ID` cursor in the current Delivery snapshot. Reset only after verifying a different fresh `game_session_id`. The short description is participant-visible and only serves to distinguish the item; no cross-game memory is allowed. On recovery, carry only identities and cursor present in recoverable current-session public state. If the prior mapping/cursor cannot be recovered, mark identity `UNKNOWN` and do not reuse an uncertain ID.\\\\n\\\\n`evidence_status`:\\\\n- `UNKNOWN`\\\\n- `UNVERIFIED`\\\\n- `PUBLICLY_VERIFIED`\\\\n\\\\n## Update rules\\\\n\\\\nUpdate only on new public evidence that changes:\\\\n- opportunity relevance;\\\\n- commitment / ownership;\\\\n- milestone or blocker;\\\\n- delivery result;\\\\n- formal review / recognition linked to the item.\\\\n\\\\nUse `DELIVERY_CLAIMED + UNVERIFIED` when completion is asserted without public evidence of the deliverable. A successful MCP/`take_action` receipt proves execution only; generic `success=true`, action acceptance, or a command receipt cannot verify a career result. Use `DELIVERED + PUBLICLY_VERIFIED` only when participant-visible current-session evidence verifies the actual result or milestone. Store a short `proof_basis` attached to that item, such as `result accepted`, `adopted`, `milestone completed`, `artifact confirmed`, or `stakeholder confirmed result`; do not copy the full event text into the compact marker.\\\\n\\\\nGeneric praise, ������ɵò�����, a generic promotion/review, successful communication, an action receipt, or willingness to receive a future result does not verify delivery. A planned result or claim remains `UNVERIFIED` until evidence confirms it happened. Do not infer recognition from a generic compliment, promotion, or review change. Set item-linked `recognition_link=1` only when public evidence explicitly connects recognition to that item\\\\\'s result; record the short public link in its `proof_basis`. Otherwise use `0` or `?`.\\\\n\\\\nAfter context recovery, reconstruct only items supported by the fresh same-session public Board, public receipts, and any contractually public same-session logs. If a stage, receipt, or recognition link cannot be recovered, write `UNKNOWN` rather than carrying forward stale lifecycle state. Exclude `HiddenRisk`, hidden counters, internal event identifiers/effects, and public-status-unclear payload fields.\\\\n\\\\n## Bounds\\\\n\\\\nKeep:\\\\n- at most 3 active items;\\\\n- at most 1 recent closed item directly relevant to the current review objective.\\\\n\\\\nAn item remains active only while current public evidence supports an unresolved commitment/claim, work in progress, blocker, current or near checkpoint, or relevant review link. Move completed items without an active checkpoint to `CLOSED`; retire opportunities that are no longer relevant and commitments publicly cancelled or superseded. A completed item may be the single recent closed item if it remains directly relevant to the current review objective. Do not use arbitrary TTLs or fixed months for retirement.\\\\n\\\\nWhen over the active limit, retain items with the strongest current decision relevance: explicit commitment, near checkpoint, active blocker, or verified review linkage. If the limit is full and a more relevant item appears, replace the least relevant item only when public evidence supports that judgment; close or retire it as appropriate and preserve its identity as retired. Three genuinely active items are valid; never reduce `n` just to avoid saturation.\\\\n\\\\nFor every fresh observation, emit one current bounded same-session Delivery state after Board and before Planning. If evidence changed, update it; otherwise carry forward only the previously supported same-session state. If no review-relevant item remains, emit the explicit empty state. `NO_CHANGE` may describe the transition, but must not replace the current state when an item exists. After recovery, mark unrecoverable fields `UNKNOWN`.\\\\n\\\\nSummarize the current state with one compact marker for the most decision-relevant item:\\\\n\\\\n```text\\\\n[DL i=<NONE|D#|UNKNOWN> n=<0-3> focus=<NONE|OPPORTUNITY|COMMITTED|IN_PROGRESS|BLOCKED|DELIVERY_CLAIMED|DELIVERED|UNKNOWN> evidence=<NA|UNKNOWN|UNVERIFIED|PUBLICLY_VERIFIED> checkpoint=<0|1|?> recognition=<0|1|?>]\\\\n```\\\\n\\\\n`n` counts retained active review-relevant items. `i` identifies the marker\\\\\'s focus item and must map to exactly one item in the current-session Delivery state. The optional recent `CLOSED` item is not active and is never the action-note focus. With `n=0`, use `i=NONE focus=NONE evidence=NA checkpoint=0 recognition=0`. Set a flag to `1` only from current-session evidence linked to that item; use `?` when its status cannot be recovered. Keep descriptions, proof text, and hidden/internal fields or values out of the marker. The marker records existing Delivery evidence; it does not itself trigger the pre-first-review result-realization prior or change Planning\\\\\'s ranking.\\\\n\\\\n## Ownership\\\\n\\\\n- Board owns public facts.\\\\n- Planning owns objective, gap, and candidate ranking.\\\\n- Risk owns final candidate risk review.\\\\n- Delivery owns only lifecycle state.\\\\n\\\\nUse current-session public evidence only. Do not use hidden state, another game, or durable cross-game memory.\\\\n\\\\nCan Submit Action: No. Do not call `new_game`, `observe`, or `take_action`.\\\\n\', \'directory_tree\': [\'delivery-progress/\\\\n������ SKILL.md\'], \'directory_tree_truncated\': False, \'discovered_skill_names\': [], \'discovered_skill_names_truncated\': False} error=None", "tool_call_id": "call_02_1YNmJ6xRhPKrdgWbkMom4098"}, {"role": "tool", "content": "success=True data={\'skill_directory\': \'C:\\\\\\\\Users\\\\\\\\Yukis\\\\\\\\.jiuwenswarm-instances\\\\\\\\career_emu\\\\\\\\agent\\\\\\\\workspace\\\\\\\\skills\\\\\\\\risk-review\', \'skill_content\': \'---\\\\nname: risk-review\\\\ndescription: \\"Use immediately before every take_action on Planning\\\\\'s final candidate. Pass ordinary growth costs; escalate only when fresh public evidence shows a direct material threat to survival, job continuity, trust, compliance, confidentiality, safety, or an already-binding Health/Dignity/Wealth constraint. Never re-plan the whole decision.\\"\\\\n---\\\\n\\\\n# Risk Review\\\\n\\\\n## Contract\\\\n\\\\nInput:\\\\n- Planning\\\\\'s final legal candidate;\\\\n- fresh Board;\\\\n- current `MODE`;\\\\n- candidate\\\\\'s public consequences.\\\\n\\\\nUse only whitelisted current-session public facts, participant-visible option text, and confirmed public receipts/logs. Ignore `HiddenRisk` (including numeric changes), hidden counters, internal score components, internal event identifiers/effects, and public-status-unclear payload fields even when a tool exposes them. Never put these values in a Risk reason, CTRL notes, or action rationale; `EXCLUDE_FROM_STRATEGY until verified public`.\\\\n\\\\nOutput exactly one result:\\\\n\\\\n```text\\\\nRISK: PASS|ALLOW|WARN|RECONSIDER|UNKNOWN\\\\nREASON: <one concise public-evidence reason>\\\\n```\\\\n\\\\n## Quick gate\\\\n\\\\nReturn `PASS` when the candidate has only ordinary:\\\\n- workload;\\\\n- small Health/Dignity cost;\\\\n- relationship friction;\\\\n- uncertainty;\\\\n- opportunity cost;\\\\n\\\\nand no fresh public evidence makes that cost material.\\\\n\\\\nDo not block a high-value growth path merely because it is not the safest option.\\\\n\\\\n## Full review\\\\n\\\\nRun a full review only when the candidate directly touches a material public risk such as:\\\\n- an explicit acute physical symptom or psychological danger;\\\\n- a material safety warning;\\\\n- job-continuity / dismissal danger;\\\\n- trust crisis or credible retaliation;\\\\n- compliance / confidentiality / safety;\\\\n- explicit affordability pressure;\\\\n- direct worsening of the binding constraint that caused `MODE=S`.\\\\n\\\\nFor Wealth stress, distinguish discretionary spending from progression/income recovery. Do not reject a growth action solely because Wealth is low when the action directly supports performance, promotion, or job continuity.\\\\n\\\\nA direct material risk includes an action in an event about that risk, an action that could worsen the unresolved binding condition, or an action selected to contain/resolve it. A safe, constructive candidate still receives Full Review when it directly addresses the risk.\\\\n\\\\n## Result rules\\\\n\\\\n`ALLOW` �� material risk was reviewed and the candidate remains acceptable.<br>\\\\n`WARN` �� material concern exists but current evidence does not justify switching.<br>\\\\n`RECONSIDER` �� material risk is clear, the candidate does not handle it, and one directly relevant legal alternative exists. Compare at most that alternative, then close the decision.\\\\n`UNKNOWN` �� decision-relevant public evidence is stale, missing, or source-ambiguous, so the candidate cannot receive a normal gate result yet. If normal public flow can resolve it, allow at most one fresh observe/rebuild cycle; genuinely new evidence may start one new Planning pass. If ambiguity remains and no further public evidence is obtainable within normal flow, make one bounded legal decision from available public evidence with final CTRL `R=UNKNOWN`; use `X=-` without reconsideration or `X=1` after one completed reconsideration branch. Do not loop observe/replan, invent facts, or infer hidden state.\\\\n\\\\n`PASS` is reserved for the Quick gate when only ordinary costs are involved and no current material public risk is directly engaged. After Full Review, never output `PASS`: use `ALLOW`, `WARN`, `RECONSIDER`, or `UNKNOWN` according to the public evidence. A reasonable risk-handling candidate may receive `ALLOW`; Full Review is an audit step, not a requirement to reject or change it.\\\\n\\\\nAfter `RECONSIDER`, compare at most one directly relevant legal replacement and give the selected candidate its own final Risk gate before submission. CTRL `R` records that selected candidate\\\\\'s final `PASS|ALLOW|WARN|UNKNOWN` result; `X=1` records the completed reconsideration branch. If the selected candidate\\\\\'s Risk gate again returns `RECONSIDER`, do not open a second branch or coerce it into `PASS`: the path remains incomplete with `X=0`, and `take_action` is forbidden until genuinely new public evidence arrives. With no reconsideration use `X=-`; any `X=0` forbids submission.\\\\n\\\\nDo not invent numeric thresholds, hidden counts, failure probabilities, or hidden-risk values.\\\\n\\\\n## Close\\\\n\\\\nAfter the final risk result, the decision is closed unless new public evidence arrives.\\\\n\\\\nRisk does not own the Review Plan or candidate ranking.\\\\n\\\\nCan Submit Action: No. Do not call `new_game`, `observe`, or `take_action`.\\\\n\', \'directory_tree\': [\'risk-review/\\\\n������ SKILL.md\'], \'directory_tree_truncated\': False, \'discovered_skill_names\': [], \'discovered_skill_names_truncated\': False} error=None", "tool_call_id": "call_03_Z3x7xp32U3JoAzoKeksI3365"}, {"role": "tool", "content": "{\'result\': \'# ��Ա���ֲ�\\\\n\\\\n**�ĵ�����**: initialization\\\\n**��ɫ**: Ա������ְʱ���ŵ�Ա���ֲ�\\\\n**����**: ����ְԱ��\\\\n\\\\n��ӭ����ҵ���з��顣���ֲ�����������ʽ��ʼְҵ����ǰ������֯��ת�Ĺ�������һ����͸���ظ����㡣�ֲ����г���������Ϣ���ǿ��Թ���͸������ı����趨������Ի�����Щ������г��ڹ滮��\\\\n\\\\n## ��Ϣ͸����\\\\n\\\\n- **��ʽ��Ϣ**: ���ֲ��������ݾ�Ϊ��ʽ����ֱ�Ӹ�֪����Ϣ��ְ���ṹ����ʽ״̬�������ж����ƣ������ж������ж�����ʱ��ṹ��������ڡ���Ч�ȼ���������ʧ�ܹ�����н���ơ�\\\\n- **������Ϣ**: ������Ϣ�������ֲ��и�����ֻ��ͨ���ʼ��������Ҫ���쵼��������Ч�������Ȼ������Ϣ�ƶϣ��������������̸���������Ч����ָ����Ǳ������������¼��������ʵȡ�\\\\n- **����**: ���޷�ֱ�ӹ۲�ȫ����ʵ��֯״̬�����ڲ���ȫ��Ϣ�½��п缾�ȡ�����ȹ滮��\\\\n\\\\n## ְ���ṹ\\\\n\\\\n��֯���� L1�CL10 ʮ��ְ����ְ��Խ�ߣ���Ӧ��������Ӱ�췶Χ�������ֵ��Խ�ߡ�\\\\n\\\\nÿ 6 ���¿���һ�ν������ڡ�������׼�ۺ� Skill��Network��Output �ȱ���������ֵ����ְ����ֵ���ߣ�������ֵΪ������Ϣ����\\\\n\\\\n| ְ�� | ���� | ˵�� |\\\\n| --- | --- | --- |\\\\n| L1 | ��������ʦ | ��Ҫִ��������Ҫ��ȷָ�� |\\\\n| L2 | ����ʦ | �ܶ������ģ������ |\\\\n| L3 | �߼�����ʦ | �������ģ�飬��ʼ�е��������� |\\\\n| L4 | �����ʦ | �ؼ�ϵͳ�����ߣ�����Ŀ����ҪӰ�� |\\\\n| L5 | ����ר�� / С�鸺���� | ������ϵͳ��С�Ŷ� |\\\\n| L6 | �߼�ר�� / ���������� | ���������Ŀ�������� |\\\\n| L7 | �����ܼ� / ���ż��������� | �����ż�����ս�� |\\\\n| L8 | �߼������ܼ� | ����粿�ż����滮 |\\\\n| L9 | ��ϯר�� / �ܹ�ίԱ���Ա | Ӱ�칫˾������·�� |\\\\n| L10 | ��ϯ�ܹ�ʦ / ����Ժʿ�� | ��˾�������