 -1, Dignity -1\\n- ����ѧϰ: 2 energy\\n\\nGiven Health=3 is low, I\'ll do: �����ָ� (1) + ����ѧϰ (2)? That gives Health +2-1 = +1 (net 4), Skill +1. Or �����ָ� (1) + ׼���㱨���� (1) + ����ά�� (1) = Health +2, Output +1, Dignity +1, Network +1, Dignity +1 = total 3 energy. That\'s balanced: H 3��5, O +1, N +1, D +2.\\n\\nHmm. Let me think about progression. We\'re L1, pre-first-review. Skill is 9 already. Output is 1 (dropped). The promotion is based on Skill/Network/Output.\\n\\nActually wait, Skill 9 seems high. The primary gap pre-review is UNKNOWN. Broad growth.\\n\\nGiven Health concern, let me allocate:\\n- �����ָ� (choice 6): 1 energy, Health +2\\n- ����ѧϰ (choice 2): 2 energy, Skill +1, Health -1\\n\\nNet: Health 3+2-1 = 4, Skill +1. Total 3 energy. That keeps health from crashing and boosts skill.\\n\\nAlternatively:\\n- �����ָ� (1): H +2\\n- ׼���㱨���� (1): O +1, D +1\\n- ����ά�� (1): N +1, D +1\\nNet: H 3��5, O+1, N+1, D+2. This improves more dimensions.\\n\\nHmm. Which is better? Skill is already 9, high. Output is low (1). Network is low (2). For promotion (Skill/Network/Output thresholds), Network and Output are the deficits. So boosting Network and Output might be more valuable than more Skill.\\n\\nBut health is the survival floor. Let me prioritize health recovery (1 energy, +2 health) then use 2 energy on progression.\\n\\nActually, the skill says: at first Energy decision of a quarter, set QUARTER_INTENT. Submit Energy one integer at a time. After each action, fresh observe. Replan remaining Energy only after material new evidence.\\n\\nSo I should submit energy actions one at a time. Let me start with health recovery since Health=3 is the most urgent (survival floor).\\n\\nActually, wait �� \\"Submit Energy one integer at a time. After each action, fresh observe. Replan the remaining Energy only after material new evidence.\\"\\n\\nSo I pick one energy action, submit it (choice), observe, then decide next.\\n\\nLet me start with �����ָ� (choice 6) to 