f. The skill says \\"When no material constraint exists, give a strong prior to broad-growth options that combine visible ownership with multiple public progression gains.\\"\\n\\nOption A: dinner (Network warmth) �� but does it give multiple gains? Relationship + possibly demo.\\nOption B: lunch + demo �� Output/ownership + relationship.\\n\\nHmm. I think B is the more balanced/efficient: it combines the demo (Output, ownership) with a face-to-face working meal (Network). A adds an extra 2h dinner �� more warmth but more cost.\\n\\nActually the description says B is \\"������� + ������ demo ʱ��һ���԰Ѻ������������\\". So B includes the demo AND a working lunch. A is dinner only (the demo presumably separate). Hmm, actually the demo is your responsibility in all cases.\\n\\nI\'ll go with B: it combines the technical demo (core delivery/ownership) with a face-to-face working meal, efficient and compliant, lower cost. Actually, wait �� but is the dinner (A) more valuable for a \\"��Ҫ�ͻ�\\"? \\n\\nLet me just decide: Given health is a concern (4) and the core value is the demo, and Network warmth can be built via the working lunch, I choose B as the balanced progression choice with multiple gains (Output via demo + Network via face-to-face) at moderate cost.\\n\\nHmm, but actually reconsider: A \\"��������������Ͳ����2Сʱ\\" �� the dinner is also face-to-face relationship building, plus you\'re the demo owner anyway. The difference is just A = dinner (evening, 2h) vs B = lunch + afternoon demo.\\n\\nI think the strongest career play for an important client you own is to invest in the relationship �� but the demo matters most. Both A and B deliver the demo. A adds warmth.\\n\\nOK let me just go with B �� it\'s efficient, compliant, combines demo + working meal, and is a strong multi-gain option without excess cost. Actually...\\n\\nHmm, let me reconsider one more time with the \\"aggressive advancement\\" default. If A and B both deliver the demo, and A additionally builds 