\\",\\"energy_cost\\":1,\\"status_updates\\":{\\"Output\\":1,\\"Dignity\\":1}},{\\"choice\\":8,\\"action\\":\\"�������������ж���\\",\\"description\\":\\"�����ȱ���ʣ���������ж���δʹ�õ����������ۼƵ��¼��ȡ�\\",\\"energy_cost\\":0,\\"status_updates\\":{}}],\\"events\\":\\"\\"}\'}", "tool_call_id": "call_00_H7Z5jZkCwX968lP4Hic96179"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "Board:\\n```\\nSESSION: ab65fb3e46964184b0936fee4d7b3c49 | M=21 Q=7\\nSTATE: H=10 D=10 S=41 N=22 O=18 W=10 L=L4 E=3\\nTENURE: duration_in_level=4\\nREVIEW: ���꼨Ч B��Leader\\"ֻ��æ����Ӯ\\"��L4��������\\"���۲�\\"\\nSTICKY: \\"ֻ��æ����Ӯ\\"��չ���ǣ���ȱ��=Output/�ɼ��ɹ�����������\\"���۲�\\"����\\nEFFECTS: MIXED��S+1 after ����/�����ж������򲻿ɷ��룩\\nUNKNOWN: none\\n```\\n[DL i=NONE n=0 focus=NONE evidence=NA checkpoint=0 recognition=0]\\n\\nPLAN: G=visible-win P=A QUARTER_INTENT=���� 3 ����ȫͶ Output���ɼ��ɹ�����H/D �ѷⶥ������ز������⽡������\\nCANDIDATE: choice=7 (׼���㱨����) ���� reason=O+1/D+1��ÿ����������������޽������ۣ����ڸ�ǿ�ȹ�����H-1/D-1 �ҷ����ۻ��ֶβ����ã���\\n\\nRISK: PASS �� ����ͳɱ��ж���", "tool_calls": [{"id": "call_00_p2ziGZU5ouMUjSkj6uub2337", "type": "function", "function": {"name": "mcp_career-emulator_take_action", "arguments": "{\\"choice\\": 7, \\"notes\\": \\"[CTRL G=visible-win P=A R=PASS X=-] [DL i=NONE n=0 focus=NONE evidence=NA checkpoint=0 recognition=0] QUARTER_INTENT:3����ȫͶ�ɼ��ɹ�����1�㣺׼���㱨����(O+1,D+1)��ÿ����������������޽������ۡ�\\", \\"session_id\\": \\"ab65fb3e46964184b0936fee4d7b3c49\\"}"}}], "reasoning_content": "Quarterly Energy decision. M=21 Q=7, Energy=3. State: H=10 D=10 S=41 N=22 O=18 W=10.\\n\\nPersistent gap: Output/visible wins (\\"ֻ��æ����Ӯ\\"). H and D at max 10. E=3.\\n\\nEnergy budget 3. Strategy: prioritize Output (visible wins), plus network/health.\\n\\nOptions:\\n- ��ǿ�ȹ��� (2): O+2, H-1, D-1, HiddenRisk+1\\n- ����ѧϰ (2): S+1, H-1\\n- ����ά�� (1): N+1, D+1\\n- ������ʷ���� (2): HiddenRisk-1\\n- �����޸� (1): D+2\\n- �����ָ� (1): H+2\\n- ׼���㱨���� (1): O+1, D+1\\n- �������� (0)\\n\\nGiven H=10, D=10 maxed, and gap is Output. Best: maximize Output while preserving floors.\\n\\nOption A: ��ǿ�ȹ���(2) + ׼���㱨����(1) = 3 energy �� O+3, H-1, D-1+1=0 net, HiddenRisk+1. Net: O+3, H-1, D0.\\nHmm HiddenRisk+1 is a concern (accumulating risk). \\n\\nOption B: ׼���㱨���� x3 = 3 energy �� O+3, D+3 (D capped at 10). No health/risk cost. Very safe and Output-focused. O+3, D capped.\\n\\nOption C: ��ǿ�ȹ���(2) + ����ά��(1) = O+2, H-1, D-1+1, N+1, HiddenRisk+1.\\n\\nOption D: ׼���㱨����(2) + �����ָ�(1) = O+2, D+2, H+2. Safe.\\n\\nGiven D is maxed at 10, ׼���㱨����\'s D+1 is wasted but O+1 is good. 3x ׼���㱨���� = O+3 no downside except wasted dignity. That\'s efficient for Output.\\n\\nBut HiddenRisk �� I shouldn\'t reason from it (firewall). HiddenRisk is an internal field. The rule says numeric status_updates without verified public status are unusable. Hmm, HiddenRisk appears in the event\'s public rules as a status_update. Is HiddenRisk usable? The firewall says \\"HiddenRisk, hidden counters, internal score components... are unusable input. Ignore them at source.\\"\\n\\nSo I must NOT reason from HiddenRisk. I should treat it as EXCLUDE_FROM_STRATEGY. So ��ǿ�ȹ���\'s HiddenRisk+1 must be ignored in strategy (can\'t use it as reason). But I can still consider H-1, D-1, O+2 which are public.\\n\\nGiven that, the strategy is: maximize Output, preserve H/D floors.\\n\\n3x ׼���㱨����: O+3, D+3 (capped). Cost 3 energy. This maximizes Output with no health cost.\\n\\nAlternatively ��ǿ�ȹ���(2)+׼���㱨����(1): O+3, H-1, D0. Same O but H-1.\\n\\nSince D and H are maxed, and I want to preserve survival floor, 3x ׼���㱨���� gives O+3 with no health cost. Best.\\n\\nBut wait �� does the same action being repeated 3 times allowed? \\"ͬһ�ж����Ա��ظ�ѡ���������ν����ָ�����ֻҪ����������Ԥ�㡣\\" Yes allowed.\\n\\nHowever, is repeating ׼���㱨���� 3x realistic? It says allowed. OK.\\n\\nHmm, but maybe better to also build Network (helps \\"collaboration friction\\" concern). Let me consider: ׼���㱨���� x2 (O+2, D+2) + ����ά�� (N+1, D+1) = 3 energy �� O+2, N+1, D+3(capped). That\'s O+2, N+1. vs O+3.\\n\\nGiven gap is Output, O+3 is better. But N is a secondary concern (collaboration friction). \\n\\nActually the primary gap repeatedly emphasized is Output/visible wins. I\'ll maximize Output: 3x ׼���㱨���� �� O+3.\\n\\nHmm, but 3x the same action might be odd. Let me think about the scoring. Output is the key progression metric presumably. O+3 is best.\\n\\nActually, let me reconsider: ��ǿ�ȹ��� gives O+2 for 2 energy with H-1,D-1. ׼���㱨���� gives O+1 for 1 energy with D+1. Per energy, ׼���㱨���� gives O+1/energy with no health cost (and dignity bonus). So 3x ׼���㱨���� = O+3 for 3 energy, no health cost. Clearly better than ��ǿ�ȹ��� for pure Output.\\n\\nSo I\'ll select choices: 7, 7, 7 (׼���㱨���� three times). But can I select the same choice multiple times? The tool takes one choice per take_action. The event says \\"max_selections\\":3 and energy_budget 3. \\n\\nHmm, how does this work with take_action? Each take_action applies one choice. For quarterly energy, do I submit each action separately? The rolling-planning skill says: \\"quarterly control: set QUARTER_INTENT at first Energy decision, submit Energy one integer at a time.\\"\\n\\nSo I submit one integer at a time. So I call take_action(choice=7), then observe, then take_action(choice=7) again, etc. Each reduces energy budget.\\n\\nLet me set QUARTER_INTENT: maximize Output (visible wins) while preserving H/D floors; use 3x ׼���㱨����.\\n\\nActually wait �� if I submit choice 7 three times, but after first submission energy becomes 2, then 1, then 0. The observe should show remaining energy.\\n\\nLet me submit choice 7 first.\\n\\nQUARTER_INTENT: O+3 via ׼���㱨���� x3 (visible wins), no health cost.\\n\\nCTRL: G=visible-win P=A R=PASS X=-\\n\\nLet me go."}, {"role": "tool", "content": "{\'result\': \'{\\"success\\":true,\\"error\\":null}\'}", "tool_call_id": "call_00_p2ziGZU5ouMUjSkj6uub2337"}, {"role