ewer raw messages, fresh tool results, and the latest user instructions override this summary.\\n</conflict_policy>\\n<summary>\\n### 1. Active Task\\n- Latest user request (web, zh): ��ʼһ���µ�ְҵģ������Ϸ������ IDENTITY.md �еĹ�����Ѱ�װ���ܽ�����Ϸ��\\n  - Recommended steps: (1) call `show_employee_handbook` once; (2) call `new_game`, print `SESSION_ID=<session_id>`; (3) loop `observe` �� ���� �� `take_action` until game ends; (4) when game ends, print the full `ending_score` content, then output `DONE`.\\n- Success criteria: play the full 48-month game to termination using the four skills; on game end, output complete `ending_score` and the literal token `DONE`.\\n- Snapshot scoped to this active play round; earlier context (handbook, skill contracts) is background that must still be honored.\\n\\n### 2. Constraints and Preferences\\n- IDENTITY.md: You are the \\"ְ��ģ���� AI ���\\". Sole task = use installed skills to fully play one career-emulator game and maximize score.\\n- Installed skills (read once at start; do NOT reread each turn): `structured-state-board`, `rolling-planning`, `delivery-progress`, `risk-review`.\\n- Participant strategy (binding):\\n  - GLOBAL EVIDENCE FIREWALL: HiddenRisk, hidden counters, internal score components, internal event ids/effects, unverified numeric status_updates, and public-status-unclear fields are UNUSABLE �� ignore at source, never quote/compare/summarize/reason from them, including internally. Only approved public evidence may enter Board/Planning/Delivery/Risk/CTRL/DL/action rationale; mark restricted data `EXCLUDE_FROM_STRATEGY until verified public`. Never infer hidden thresholds/caps/weights or event��answer lookups.\\n  - Single Agent is the only action submitter. Board=facts; Planning=strategy/ranking; Delivery=lifecycle; Risk=final gate.\\n  - Flow: fresh observe �� Board �� Delivery �� Planning �� Risk �� preflight �� take_action �� fresh observe �� continue.\\n  - WHOLE-GAME EXECUTION: after every successful take_action, immediately obtain a fresh observe and begin the next decision cycle. Do not stop after one action/month/quarter/review/promotion/decision-closure. DECISION_CLOSED closes only current action selection, not execution. Continue until structured game state says game ended or unrecoverable tool failure. Do not send a voluntary terminal user-facing answer while game active.\\n  - ACTION PREFLIGHT before each take_action: confirm current game_session_id; exactly one legal integer choice; Planning closed on exactly one candidate; final Risk review complete; valid CTRL and DL markers in notes. Notes must begin with exactly one `[CTRL G=<gap|?> P=<A|S|?> R=<PASS|ALLOW|WARN|UNKNOWN> X=<0|1|->]` followed by exactly one `[DL i=<NONE|D#|UNKNOWN> n=<0-3> focus=<...> evidence=<...> checkpoint=<...> recognition=<...>]`. CTRL R always records the selected submitted candidate\'s final Risk result. X=0 forbids submission.\\n  - CONTEXT RECOVERY: on compaction/resume, mark RECOVERY_PENDING; confirm same session_id; fresh observe; reread all four skills; rebuild Board/Delivery/Review Plan from whitelisted current-session public facts; emit RECOVERY_READY only after all confirmed, then resume. If identity/observe/skill-reread cannot be confirmed, stay RECOVERY_PENDING and do not act.\\n- Core rules: NEVER call `new_game` twice if a session_id exists. Never stop/ask user before game ends. Prefer observe before deciding; don\'t guess state.\\n- Output discipline: complete deliverables must be in the final no-tool message; status-only confirmations are not enough.\\n- Environment: win32, PowerShell available; Git Bash available. Respond in Simplified Chinese.\\n\\n### 3. Completed Work in This Active Segment\\n- Read all four SKILL.md files once.\\n- Called `show_employee_handbook` once.\\n- Started game: `new_game` �� SESSION_ID=ab65fb3e46964184b0936fee4d7b3c49 (printed to user).\\n- Executed a continuous loop of observe �� (Board/Delivery/Planning/Risk) �� take_action with proper `[CTRL ...]` and `[DL ...]` notes, from month 1 through month 45 (year 4), through multiple half-year reviews and promotions L1��L2��L3��L4��L5.\\n- Every take_action returned `{\'success\': True, \'error\': None}`; a fresh observe was fetched after each.\\n- Latest completed action: at M=45 Q=15, submitted choice 7 (׼���㱨����) as the 1st of the quarter\'s 3 Energy actions (QUARTER_INTENT: Output Ϊ�����ɳ�ά�ȣ�3 ����ȫͶ Output). take_action returned success=true. Fresh observe had NOT yet been fetched when this checkpoint was requested.\\n\\n### 4. Current Work and Active State\\n- Session: ab65fb3e46964184b0936fee4d7b3c49. Time: M=45, Q=15, year 4 (48-month game; ~3 months remaining).\\n- Last fresh observe BEFORE the just-submitted action (M=45 Q=15, quarterly Energy allocation, energy_budget=3):\\n  - H=10 D=10 S=123 N=54 O=38 W=35 L=L5 E=3; duration_in_level=10.\\n- Latest Board (last recorded):\\n  - REVIEW: ���꼨Ч A��+1.5����Leader\\"�ܿ��¡������ڰ칫�����Ρ��ѹ����ڲ����͹�ϵ�ϣ�������ٿ�һ��\\"���ѽ��� L5���ѽ���ܹ��飨CTO ������ῴ����������ڣ���\\n  - STICKY: �����ȶ���10�������ش�δ�����ա�\\n- Delivery: n=0 (no tracked review-relevant work items; marker `[DL i=NONE n=0 focus=NONE evidence=NA checkpoint=0 recognition=0]`).\\n- MODE mostly A; briefly S (M=36) when health fell to 5 (����Լ��), then returned to A after health restored to 10. Health has since oscillated (dropped to 8 twice via relationship-building/social actions, restored via �����ָ�).\\n\\n### 5. Immediate Resume Point\\n- Last concrete action: `take_action(session_id=ab65fb3e46964184b0936fee4d7b3c49, choice=7, notes=\\"[CTRL G=visible-win P=A R=PASS X=-] [DL i=NONE n=0 focus=NONE evidence=NA checkpoint=0 recognition=0] QUARTER_INTENT:Output������3����ȫͶ�ɼ��ɹ�����1�㣺׼���㱨����(O+1,D+1)��\\")` �� returned `{\'success\': True, \'error\': None}`.\\n- Next step: call `observe(session_id=ab65fb3e46964184b0936fee4d7b3c49)` to get fresh state, then continue the standard decision cycle (Board �� Delivery �� Planning �� Risk �� pre